{title: I Praise You, My Father}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 99}

Lyrics
[Bm7](8 Measure Introduction)

Verse 1
I [D]praise You, my [A]Father,
[Bm7]In Your unchanging [F#m]grace.
My [G]very life [D]You do [D]sustain.
[D]In service [A]and honor,
[Bm]In living [F#m]every day,
[G]Your praise and [D]glory I [Bm]proclaim.

Chorus 1
[Dmaj7]Until Your [B7]kingdom [D]comes,
I [E7]pray [A7]Your [D]will be done;
May [Bm7]all creation [Dmaj7]praise
Your holy [B]name.

Verse 2
[Bm7]I [D]praise You, [A]my Father,
[Bm7]In Your [F#m7]undying [Dmaj7]love
[F#m]That [G]reaches out [D]and shows [Bm7]the Way.
[A]You [D]sought me, and [A]found me,
[Bm]And brought me [F#m]safely home;
You [G]turned my [D]darkness into [Bm7]day.

Chorus 2
[F#m7]I give you [D]everything;
hold [Em]nothing in [D]reserve.
[Bm7]My heart [Bm7]and [D]soul [F#m]I bring
[D]to carry [G]out [D]your Word.
[Bm7]To You alone [F#m]I call;
[Bm]You [Em7]are my Lord, [D]my All.
A living [Dmaj7]sacrifice
I'll [Em7]be for [F#]You.
[G]Verse 3 and [D]Ending
I praise You, [A]my Father,
[Bm]In Your unchanging [F#m]grace.
[G]My very life [D]You do [B7]sustain.
[F#m7]In [D]service and [A]honor,
[Bm]In [Bm]living every [F#m]day,
[D]Your praise and [G]glory I [A]proclaim.
[E7]Your [Em]praise and glory [A]I [E]proclaim.
